Package: devjam-science-opensesame-rt
Version: 1.0-1
Section: science
Priority: optional
Architecture: all
Depends: python3-opensesame
Recommends: devjam-system-config-lowlatency
Suggests: devjam-science-experiment-mode
Maintainer: Bob Rosbag <debian@bobrosbag.nl>
Description: OpenSesame launcher with real-time priority
 A desktop launcher that starts OpenSesame from the python3-opensesame
 package as a user service with real-time priority. In experiment mode
 (devjam-science-experiment-mode) that OpenSesame runs on the isolated CPU
 cores; manage-opensesame-rt-affinity sets other CPUs.
 .
 The service needs the real-time limits of devjam-system-config-lowlatency
 (rtprio 95 and unlimited memlock for the audio group); without them it
 does not start. This package does for the OpenSesame installed with apt
 what devjam-science-opensesame-psychopy does for the one in the PsychoPy
 environment in /opt/psychopy.
